249
00:20:54,169 --> 00:20:56,338
Two of these. Three of these.

250
00:20:59,883 --> 00:21:02,219
Almost done. Last one.

251
00:21:06,014 --> 00:21:07,307
That's it. Done.

252
00:21:12,354 --> 00:21:13,563
Shit.

253
00:21:48,557 --> 00:21:50,309
Are you done already?

254
00:21:50,392 --> 00:21:54,021
I'm done with inventory. I'm done, but…

255
00:21:54,104 --> 00:21:55,355
But what?

256
00:21:55,439 --> 00:21:58,400
There's someone…

257
00:21:58,483 --> 00:22:00,610
No, there's something in there.

258
00:22:01,111 --> 00:22:02,988
A person. No, it's not a person.

259
00:22:03,071 --> 00:22:06,325
- What? You're scaring me!
- Something's trapped in the fridge there.

260
00:22:06,408 --> 00:22:10,245
It has a human face,
but the body is a fucking insect!

261
00:22:10,329 --> 00:22:11,872
The body is a fucking insect…

262
00:22:12,372 --> 00:22:13,790
The body is a fucking insect?

263
00:22:14,291 --> 00:22:16,460
- No.
- The body is a fucking…

264
00:22:16,543 --> 00:22:19,463
I must be seeing things because I'm tired.

265
00:22:19,546 --> 00:22:22,716
No, maybe it's a doll or something.
This must be a hidden camera prank.

266
00:22:22,799 --> 00:22:25,385
Hee-dong, look for cameras.

267
00:22:26,178 --> 00:22:27,137
Bro.

268
00:22:28,555 --> 00:22:29,806
It's not a doll.

269
00:22:32,726 --> 00:22:33,810
It's a curse.

270
00:22:36,646 --> 00:22:39,900
Ever heard of the Curse of the Chimera?
I saw it on a horror channel.

271
00:22:39,983 --> 00:22:42,194
You get mixed
with the two nearest creatures.

272
00:22:42,277 --> 00:22:47,115
That's what happens when you get mixed
with a flea on your clothes and a parrot.

273
00:22:49,242 --> 00:22:50,369
For real.

274
00:23:01,171 --> 00:23:03,799
Are you some kind of occult fanatic?

275
00:23:03,882 --> 00:23:06,009
How are you not scared of what's going on?

276
00:23:06,093 --> 00:23:06,927
Bro.

277
00:23:07,010 --> 00:23:09,930
Don't you know
there are ghosts everywhere these days?

278
00:23:10,430 --> 00:23:11,765
There's one right behind you.

279
00:23:15,936 --> 00:23:18,480
Bro, I'm just messing with you.

280
00:23:18,980 --> 00:23:20,524
You scared me even more.

281
00:23:23,819 --> 00:23:25,695
If you'd only seen the thing inside.

282
00:23:30,575 --> 00:23:31,451
Bro.

283
00:23:35,747 --> 00:23:39,835
In a situation like this, you know
what'd be a thriller-esque plot twist?

284
00:23:39,918 --> 00:23:41,086
What now?

285
00:23:41,169 --> 00:23:43,338
That this was all
the branch manager's doing.

286
00:23:43,422 --> 00:23:45,549
As a ruse,
they wrote those ominous warnings

287
00:23:45,632 --> 00:23:47,968
to suggest there was a ghost
when they had…

288
00:23:50,053 --> 00:23:51,596
a trapped girl in there.

289
00:23:54,808 --> 00:23:56,643
It'd be insane if that were true.

290
00:23:57,894 --> 00:23:59,688
I never said it was a girl.

291
00:24:00,355 --> 00:24:01,189
What?

292
00:24:02,774 --> 00:24:03,608
Nothing.

293
00:24:04,109 --> 00:24:06,862
Why do you keep stopping mid-sentence?

294
00:24:08,655 --> 00:24:09,990
I should get back to work.

295
00:24:13,660 --> 00:24:14,578
CONVENIENCE STORE RULES

296
00:24:23,211 --> 00:24:26,840
"The second part-timer is not human."

297
00:24:34,264 --> 00:24:35,223
I'm getting excited.

298
00:24:35,307 --> 00:24:36,975
Shit, is this the wrong hand? Sir!

299
00:24:37,058 --> 00:24:39,436
I can come in, right?

300
00:24:46,401 --> 00:24:50,655
USE THE CROSS IN THE STORAGE ROOM
TO DEAL WITH NON-HUMAN ENTITIES

301
00:25:02,876 --> 00:25:08,715
USE THE CROSS IN THE STORAGE ROOM
TO DEAL WITH NON-HUMAN ENTITIES

302
00:25:08,840 --> 00:25:10,592
- Goddammit!
- Holy.

303
00:25:11,343 --> 00:25:13,428
This convenience store has no customers.

304
00:25:13,512 --> 00:25:17,849
I think I made a mistake
during the storage room inventory.

305
00:25:17,933 --> 00:25:18,934
I should

306
00:25:19,935 --> 00:25:20,936
go back in there.

307
00:25:21,019 --> 00:25:23,230
You're going back
into that creepy storage room?

308
00:25:25,732 --> 00:25:27,317
Tell me what needs to be done.

309
00:25:28,860 --> 00:25:30,070
I'll go do it.

310
00:25:30,862 --> 00:25:33,573
No, you said
you've never done inventory before. I'll--

311
00:25:33,657 --> 00:25:34,824
Damn.

312
00:25:37,452 --> 00:25:38,745
You're too nice.

313
00:25:39,246 --> 00:25:41,873
You'll lose out if you live like that.

314
00:26:00,392 --> 00:26:01,810
The cross.

315
00:26:03,270 --> 00:26:04,354
The cross…

316
00:26:15,532 --> 00:26:17,033
What? Why?

317
00:26:21,246 --> 00:26:23,873
The…

318
00:26:24,457 --> 00:26:28,169
The guy outside is the bad guy, isn't he?
I can take him out with this, right?

319
00:26:34,342 --> 00:26:35,802
Come on! Am I right?

320
00:26:59,618 --> 00:27:00,619
Hey!

321
00:27:01,494 --> 00:27:02,787
You…

322
00:27:04,873 --> 00:27:07,417
I don't know what you are,
but stop this and get lost!

323
00:27:10,337 --> 00:27:12,797
I need to finish this job and get paid!

324
00:27:40,283 --> 00:27:41,660
Fuck.

325
00:28:10,146 --> 00:28:11,314
Where are you going?

326
00:28:11,398 --> 00:28:13,400
Oh, the cross?

327
00:28:20,532 --> 00:28:22,158
Why are you doing this to me?

328
00:28:22,242 --> 00:28:23,326
Why do you think?

329
00:28:23,410 --> 00:28:25,412
Because there are two in a spot for one.

330
00:28:26,246 --> 00:28:28,748
What convenience store
hires two part-timers?

331
00:28:32,711 --> 00:28:35,380
Time for you to clock out.
To the other world.

332
00:28:58,069 --> 00:28:59,112
It doesn't work.

333
00:29:03,450 --> 00:29:06,202
The store rules? That's all bullshit.

334
00:29:06,786 --> 00:29:08,163
You're so naive.

335
00:29:08,663 --> 00:29:09,831
I wrote them, you know.

336
00:29:10,832 --> 00:29:12,459
From beginning to end.

337
00:29:13,126 --> 00:29:14,127
What?

338
00:29:14,210 --> 00:29:16,755
You were fooled, you idiot.

339
00:29:19,174 --> 00:29:21,468
Don't come any closer. I said, don't!

340
00:29:21,551 --> 00:29:22,844
Where are you going?

341
00:32:05,882 --> 00:32:06,716
<i>Back then, I'd…</i>

342
00:32:08,760 --> 00:32:10,803
<i>finish what I started no matter what.</i>

343
00:34:51,422 --> 00:34:55,009
<i>It's time for us to say goodbye</i>

344
00:34:55,510 --> 00:34:58,221
<i>See you next time</i>

345
00:34:59,180 --> 00:35:03,142
<i>It's time for us to say goodbye</i>

346
00:35:03,643 --> 00:35:06,354
<i>See you next time</i>

347
00:35:07,313 --> 00:35:11,901
<i>It's sad to say goodbye</i>
<i>But let's say goodbye with a smile</i>

348
00:35:11,984 --> 00:35:13,528
ALARM

349
00:35:13,653 --> 00:35:14,821
Six o'clock.

350
00:35:23,204 --> 00:35:25,832
PART-TIME JOB COMPLETED
4,012,000 WON

351
00:35:29,001 --> 00:35:30,586
Goddamn.

352
00:36:50,166 --> 00:36:52,001
HEAD OF SPIDER STAFFING AGENCY

353
00:36:55,087 --> 00:36:56,297
Hello?

354
00:36:56,380 --> 00:36:57,590
<i>Mr. Byeon Hyeok-jun?</i>

355
00:36:58,382 --> 00:37:02,303
<i>You successfully completed the job.</i>
<i>You have a knack for this.</i>

356
00:37:02,803 --> 00:37:04,597
So I did work.

357
00:37:05,431 --> 00:37:07,350
I thought I had a nightmare or something.

358
00:37:08,100 --> 00:37:09,852
<i>Come on, a nightmare?</i>

359
00:37:09,936 --> 00:37:12,772
<i>It was a part-time job.</i>
<i>A sweet gig at that.</i>

360
00:37:14,232 --> 00:37:15,149
Is this…

361
00:37:16,943 --> 00:37:18,819
what all the jobs are like?

362
00:37:20,112 --> 00:37:23,491
<i>What's important here</i>
<i>is that you got it done.</i>

363
00:37:24,200 --> 00:37:27,328
<i>Spider Staffing Agency stickers</i>
<i>aren't just anywhere.</i>

364
00:37:27,870 --> 00:37:28,746
<i>When will you come?</i>

365
00:37:28,829 --> 00:37:30,706
Right now, I'm…

366
00:37:33,209 --> 00:37:35,378
<i>Anyway, come get your money soon.</i>

367
00:37:35,878 --> 00:37:37,088
<i>I'll have it ready.</i>

368
00:37:47,431 --> 00:37:50,893
KYUNGIL GROUP
NEO WORLD

369
00:38:05,616 --> 00:38:09,120
RESIDENT REGISTRATION CARD

370
00:38:11,998 --> 00:38:13,332
"Byeon Hyeok-jun."

371
00:38:19,046 --> 00:38:20,631
We'll be seeing each other often.

372
00:42:29,964 --> 00:42:31,757
ALL NAMES, EVENTS, BRANDS,
PERSONS, AND PLACES

373
00:42:31,840 --> 00:42:33,425
DEPICTED IN THIS SERIES ARE FICTIONAL

374
00:42:33,509 --> 00:42:35,386
ANY RESEMBLANCE TO REALITY IS COINCIDENTAL

375
00:42:39,974 --> 00:42:43,394
